<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
            http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!--
      Wave 01's "box" (DESIGN §2.4, the owner's reference 2026-07): the tile's volume is two
      fully coincident cards of one stepped silhouette, offset vertically.
      The top one (line + surface) is raised by tile-depth, and from under it the lower
      BACKING peeks out below: a warm peach gradient in the same clay outline. The mechanics are
      in wave-01.css (the .pixel-tile pseudo-layers are the top card, the .pixel-slab element is the
      backing); here are the tokens, like the other edge parameters (0160). NB: token names
      in this comment are written without the double-hyphen prefix: XML forbids it inside
      comments (in CSS it is var(tile-depth) with the prefix).

      An UPDATE over the applied 0080-theme-seed-wave01 (the seed's checksum must not be touched);
      `||` merges only these keys, the rest of wave 01's token set is untouched.
      Subtracting tile-depth-color/tile-depth-light is hygiene for environments that tried
      this branch's intermediate iterations (prod has no such keys, `-` is a no-op there).

        tile-depth   NEW: the vertical offset of the "box" cards (the height of the visible
                     part of the backing).
        tile-slab-1/2 NEW: the backing's fill gradient (warm peach); the backing's outline is
                     the same dark clay border-tile around the whole perimeter.
        tile-inner / tile-inner-color NEW: a very thin LIGHT inner frame of the top
                     card (the .pixel-lid layer) around the whole perimeter; the top card has
                     no clay frame at the bottom (the light one covers it to the bottom), so the bottom edge
                     is light and the joint with the backing works without gradients. The colour is a warm cream,
                     not #ffffff: pure white is the brightest thing on the board and cold next to the peach,
                     the line "rang" from afar.
        border-tile  #cc9f8c from 0160 → #d58b69: both cards' outline is more saturated.
        tile-line    1.5px from 0160 → 2px: a more confident line, matching the "box"'s weight.
        surface-fill the bottom of the front face warms up (#fff5ee): the lid is not a white sheet.

      Wave 02 "Obscura" is deliberately untouched: its cards draw their edge themselves (border+radius),
      wave 01's layers are switched off for it (see the note "How a wave chooses its edge" in wave-01.css).
    -->
    <changeSet id="0190-wave-01-depth-tokens" author="danchuo">
        <sql><![CDATA[
UPDATE theme
SET tokens = (tokens - 'tile-depth-color' - 'tile-depth-light' - 'tile-slab-line') || $J${
  "tile-depth": "6px",
  "tile-slab-1": "#efc8b2",
  "tile-slab-2": "#dfa083",
  "tile-inner": "1.5px",
  "tile-inner-color": "#fff3e7",
  "border-tile": "#d58b69",
  "tile-line": "2px",
  "surface-fill": "linear-gradient(180deg, #ffffff 0%, #fffdfb 35%, #fff5ee 100%)"
}$J$::jsonb
WHERE key = 'wave-01';
        ]]></sql>
        <rollback><![CDATA[
UPDATE theme
SET tokens = (tokens - 'tile-depth' - 'tile-slab-1' - 'tile-slab-2' - 'tile-inner' - 'tile-inner-color') || $J${
  "border-tile": "#cc9f8c",
  "tile-line": "1.5px",
  "surface-fill": "linear-gradient(180deg, var(--bg-surface), var(--bg-surface-2))"
}$J$::jsonb
WHERE key = 'wave-01';
        ]]></rollback>
    </changeSet>
</databaseChangeLog>
